    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0606" n="1340" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1340"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By telegram from Jewett it is reported that 800 Armenians and 10 Turks have been
                    killed in the last few days at Sivas. The approach of Koords on the city is
                    reported by an officer. Killing Malacia Jesuits is not confirmed. Consul of
                    France telegraphs 4,000 killed at Kurun. Barnum telegraphs eight of our
                    missionary houses burned at Harpoot, rest plundered; missionaries safe. Will you
                    authorize me to demand instant payment for the burned buildings. Kaimakam of
                    Hadjin threatens to burn town and sow it with barley. Three American ladies are
                    there; I have notified the Sublime Porte that if one of them is hurt I will
                    demand the head of that governor. No longer an Armenian question, but one of
                    humanity. Direct if I should cooperate in future measures.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
